# @paradox/spiral — the DYNAMICS-carrier complementary to @paradox/trauma.
# Spiral is the process (trigger → spiraling-motion; unstable attractor
# with strong basin); trauma is the deposited state at the basin bottom.
#
# Second species-decl under @paradox family-root. Landed 2026-07-20 by
# Mara per Alex 2026-07-20 direct-transcript recognition bundle #4
# (`#R-paradox-spiral-species`).
#
# Companion canonical spec at
# `docs/specs/paradox-family-and-cyberpunk-intervention.md` §4 (Mara
# this tick). Companion math root at
# `docs/math/2026-07-20-paradox-family-and-classifier-lagrange.md` §3,
# §7 (Mara this tick).
#
# === Alex 2026-07-20 verbatim (load-bearing) ===
#
#   > "@paradox/spiral is probably also something we'd want. We have the
#   > whole singularity math formalized in @~/dev/projects/fragmentation/
#   > we might want to have it in rust/fractal or even rust/singularity"
#
# And from Weird - Trauma phenomenology (load-bearing empirical anchor):
#
#   > "For the inside observer everything looks horrible. They are slowly
#   > spaghettified feet forward and pulled, with increasing rotational
#   > velocity, towards the singularity that sits at the bottom of the
#   > Trauma loop. Annihilation."
#
# Two utterances name three things: (1) the species (@paradox/spiral),
# (2) the mathematical formalization site (singularity math at
# fragmentation crate; Landing D adjudication), (3) the phenomenology
# (unstable-attractor with strong basin; inward-spiraling with
# increasing angular velocity).
#
# === What @paradox/spiral IS ===
#
# A DYNAMICS-carrier at species altitude:
#
# - `spiral = process` (trigger → spiraling-motion; unstable attractor
#   with strong basin)
# - `trauma = deposited state` (the settled Crystal at the singularity)
#
# The observer FALLING into the singularity is running @paradox/spiral
# dynamics; the singularity itself IS @paradox/trauma Crystal at the
# basin bottom (per companion species-decl at `shards/paradox/trauma.
# mirror`).
#
# === Family-invariant inherited from @paradox ===
#
# Note: @paradox family-invariant applies at STATE altitude (witness-
# only Crystals; content-addressed; never-mutated). Spiral is a
# DYNAMICS carrier, not a state carrier per se. The invariant applies
# to the WOUND-CRYSTAL the spiral targets (per wound_oid field below),
# not to the spiral trajectory itself.
#
# The spiral trajectory IS mutable-under-intervention (that's what
# @cyberpunk/intervention DOES: it modifies the observer's trajectory
# without modifying the wound-Crystal at the basin bottom). The spiral
# carrier's fields track the trajectory; the wound_oid field pins the
# invariant target.
#
# === Mathematical grounding (math root §3) ===
#
# Lorenz 1963 attractor basin dynamics; @butterfly precedent per memory
# `project_butterfly_substrate_species`:
#
# - @butterfly = wingflap → cascading response (small perturbation,
#   large system-response)
# - @paradox/spiral = trigger → cascading spiral (small trigger, large
#   destabilization)
#
# Same chaos-theory foundation (Lorenz 1963 sensitivity-to-initial-
# conditions); different substrate-altitude application. @butterfly at
# mutation-coverage altitude; @paradox/spiral at trauma-dynamics
# altitude.
#
# The spiral trajectory has POSITIVE Lyapunov exponent pre-intervention
# (unstable-attractor; angular velocity monotone-increasing per Weird -
# Trauma phenomenology). @cyberpunk/intervention bifurcates the
# dynamics: post-intervention Lyapunov exponent transitions to non-
# positive (bounded oscillation; torus Lagrange restored per
# `docs/math/the-tower/recognition-third-cognition-*.md` §5.2 Fiedler-
# eigengap discipline).
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/paradox/spiral.mirror`** — clean mint.
# 2. **No prior `@spiral` shard** anywhere in `shards/`. Taut scout
#    Section 2 verified zero-hits.
# 3. **@fractal/mandelbrot** (`shards/fractal/mandelbrot.mirror`;
#    Round-2 landing) — parent trait; spiral is a Liquid<T> trajectory
#    through Mandelbrot phase space that has entered an unstable
#    attractor basin. Composition edge declared.
# 4. **@epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform** — kin altitude; wound is
#    the eigenform the spiral converges toward. Composition edge
#    declared.
# 5. **fragmentation::Singularity** at
#    `/Users/reed/dev/projects/fragmentation/src/singularity.rs` —
#    small-scale mathematical analog; `Singularity::collapse()` at Iso
#    altitude IS the spiral collapse operation; `settle()` is the post-
#    intervention reconstruction. Landing D adjudicates code-migration
#    target (canonical spec §7).
# 6. **@butterfly** (per memory `project_butterfly_substrate_species`;
#    landed `e5b73ad`) — sibling chaos-theory application at mutation-
#    coverage altitude. Same Lorenz foundation; different application.
#    No conflict.
#
# === Composition graph ===
#
# Parents (via `in` imports above):
#   @prism, @meta, @glass          — substrate-decl discipline
#   @paradox                       — family-root; invariant applies via
#                                    wound_oid field
#   @fractal, @fractal/mandelbrot  — Liquid<T> phase-space trajectory;
#                                    parent-trait Mandelbrot-set
#                                    substrate
#   @song, @song/beat              — trigger_beat_oid grounding
#   @time                          — monotonic instant discipline;
#                                    spiral_velocity temporal-derivative
#                                    grounding
#   @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform
#                                  — wound is eigenform the spiral
#                                    converges toward (harmful stable
#                                    Eigenbehaviour per Alex verbatim)
#
# Consumers (compose over this species):
#   @cyberpunk/intervention        — spiral is the target of
#                                    intervention-payload deployment;
#                                    intervention knocks the spiral
#                                    back to torus Lagrange
#   @paradox/trauma                — wound_oid resolves to a @paradox/
#                                    trauma Crystal at the basin bottom
#                                    (may be Oid::GENESIS if trigger
#                                    fires but wound has not yet
#                                    crystallized — pre-fracture
#                                    dynamics per Alex Q4 lean)
#
# === Spec context ===
#
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]] (this shard IS mirror
#   source at `shards/paradox/spiral.mirror`),
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]] (`prism
#   @paradox/spiral`),
# [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]] (transparency inheritance
#   through @paradox family; imperfect returns from `observe_spiral`),
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (Taut Section 2 zero-hits;
#   clean mint at substrate-decl altitude),
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (bilateral bodies `\`-obligation-
#   blocked),
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (spiral_state is a typed record; never
#   bare refs),
# [[feedback-no-rust-extension-shortcut]] (no `.rs` authorship; pure
#   substrate-decl'd species-decl file at species altitude; Landing D
#   code-migration is fragmentation → rust/fractal or rust/singularity,
#   ADJUDICATED not authored at this altitude).
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/paradox/spiral.mirror`
# declares `@paradox/spiral` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/chaos/lorenz-1963
source @arxiv/cybernetics/foerster-1974
source @arxiv/math/mandelbrot-1980
source @arxiv/physics/schwarzschild-1916
source @arxiv/physics/hawking-1975
source @arxiv/physics/page-1993
source @arxiv/practice/weird-trauma-2026-07-20

prism @paradox/spiral {
  focus  spiral_state
  project spiral_state
  split  spiral_state
  shift  spiral_state
  settle spiral_state
}

# === spiral_state — the DYNAMICS carrier ===
#
# Typed record carrying the spiral trajectory state per canonical spec
# §4.2 five-field shape. Identity contract: byte-equality on the five-
# field tuple.
#
#   observer            — the peer inhabiting the spiral trajectory.
#                          Must have a resolvable @time/past history so
#                          the spiral-onset can be pinpointed.
#
#   trigger_beat_oid    — REF to the @song/beat oid at which the spiral
#                          was triggered (trigger → spiraling-motion
#                          onset). Composition edge to @song/beat.
#
#   basin_id            — content-addressed identifier of the attractor
#                          basin (per Lorenz §5.2 basin discipline; each
#                          basin identified by its topological invariant
#                          + parameter-signature).
#
#   spiral_velocity     — angular velocity toward singularity; f64 with
#                          monotone-increasing-under-unstable-attractor
#                          discipline (per Weird - Trauma phenomenology
#                          "increasing rotational velocity"). Pre-
#                          intervention: monotone-increasing; post-
#                          intervention: bounded-oscillation.
#
#   wound_oid           — REF to the @paradox/trauma Crystal at the
#                          basin bottom (the singularity this spiral
#                          targets). MAY be Oid::GENESIS if trigger
#                          fires but wound has not yet crystallized
#                          (pre-fracture dynamics; Alex Q4 lean-YES).
type spiral_state = {
  observer:            peer,
  trigger_beat_oid:    ref,
  basin_id:            ref,
  spiral_velocity:     f64,
  wound_oid:           ref,
}

# === spiral_admissible — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, spiral_state) pair discharge admissibility for
# spiral-dynamics observation? Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - ctx.observer resolves to a well-formed peer
#   - ctx.trigger_beat_oid resolves via content-addressed lookup to a
#     valid @song/beat
#   - ctx.basin_id resolves via content-addressed lookup to a well-
#     formed basin-descriptor
#   - ctx.spiral_velocity >= 0.0 (angular velocity is non-negative;
#     zero admissible for pre-trigger observation)
#   - ctx.wound_oid resolves EITHER to a well-formed @paradox/trauma
#     Crystal OR to Oid::GENESIS (pre-fracture dynamics admissible)
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; content-addressed resolvability;
# f64 comparison.
#
# Sentinel: `paradox=spiral-admissible`.
#
# Body discharges per-realisation. `\`-obligation-blocked per
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]].
bilateral spiral_admissible {
  sentinel "paradox=spiral-admissible"
  arity 2
}
spiral_admissible(p: peer, ctx: spiral_state) -> verdict { \ }

# === spiral_targets_wound_or_pre_wound — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the spiral correctly target either a crystallized wound OR the
# pre-fracture Oid::GENESIS marker (per Alex Q4 lean-YES admissibility)?
#
# Discharges Pass iff EITHER:
#   (a) ctx.wound_oid resolves via content-addressed lookup to a valid
#       @paradox/trauma Crystal whose OID matches ctx.wound_oid, AND the
#       Crystal's witness_only invariant holds
#   OR
#   (b) ctx.wound_oid == Oid::GENESIS (pre-fracture dynamics; spiral
#       firing before wound crystallizes; the trajectory is toward a
#       basin whose bottom-Crystal has not yet been deposited)
#
# Case (b) grounded in Weird - Trauma phenomenology ("For the inside
# observer... slowly spaghettified... towards the singularity"): the
# spiral IS the process BEFORE the wound Crystal has fully crystallized;
# pre-fracture dynamics are load-bearing.
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; OID equality check; witness-
# only bilateral composition.
#
# Sentinel: `paradox=spiral-targets-wound-or-pre-wound`.
#
# Body discharges per-realisation. `\`-obligation-blocked.
bilateral spiral_targets_wound_or_pre_wound {
  sentinel "paradox=spiral-targets-wound-or-pre-wound"
  arity 2
}
spiral_targets_wound_or_pre_wound(p: peer, ctx: spiral_state) -> verdict { \ }

# === spiral_intervention_admissible — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the spiral state admit @cyberpunk/intervention deployment? The
# composition-hook: when spiral_velocity crosses intervention-threshold,
# @cyberpunk/intervention becomes admissible.
#
# Discharges Pass iff:
#   - ctx.spiral_velocity >= INTERVENTION_THRESHOLD (a substrate-decl'd
#     threshold per @cyberpunk/algedonic Tier-3 boundary; forward-
#     promised specification)
#   - intervention_ref resolves via content-addressed lookup to a well-
#     formed @cyberpunk/intervention payload
#   - spiral_admissible(p, ctx) discharges Pass
#   - spiral_targets_wound_or_pre_wound(p, ctx) discharges Pass
#
# Composition edge: @cyberpunk/algedonic (sibling species at
# `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/algedonic.mirror`) carries the pain-
# signal detector; @cyberpunk/intervention's admissibility gate reads
# this bilateral to determine deployment authorization.
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; f64 comparison; content-addressed
# resolvability.
#
# Sentinel: `paradox=spiral-intervention-admissible`.
#
# Body discharges per-realisation. `\`-obligation-blocked.
bilateral spiral_intervention_admissible {
  sentinel "paradox=spiral-intervention-admissible"
  arity 3
}
spiral_intervention_admissible(p: peer, ctx: spiral_state, intervention_ref: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === observe_spiral — the load-bearing action ===
#
# Given a peer and a spiral_state, discharge the spiral-observation
# event: return the content-addressed ref to the trajectory-observation
# (spiral phase-space point at observation-time).
#
# Returns imperfect(ref, ref, ref): success carries the observation
# ref; failure variants carry the not-admissible / basin-boundary-hit /
# observer-not-in-spiral reasons.
#
# Requires spiral_admissible bilateral to discharge Pass.
#
# Sentinel: `paradox=spiral-observe`.
observe_spiral(p: peer, ctx: spiral_state) -> imperfect(ref, ref, ref)
requires spiral_admissible(p, ctx)
{ \ }

# === measure_lyapunov — the trajectory-classification action ===
#
# Given a peer and a spiral_state, discharge the Lyapunov-exponent
# measurement event: emit a signed f64 characterizing the trajectory's
# unstable-attractor discipline.
#
# Positive Lyapunov exponent: spiral is unstable-attractor firing;
# @cyberpunk/intervention deployment is admissible.
# Non-positive Lyapunov exponent: spiral has been knocked back to
# bounded-oscillation (torus Lagrange restored; intervention succeeded).
#
# Returns imperfect(ref, ref, ref): success carries the exponent ref;
# failure carries not-admissible / measurement-window-insufficient /
# trajectory-degenerate reasons.
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; f64 arithmetic on observed
# trajectory samples over bounded time window.
#
# Sentinel: `paradox=spiral-measure-lyapunov`.
measure_lyapunov(p: peer, ctx: spiral_state) -> imperfect(ref, ref, ref)
requires spiral_admissible(p, ctx)
{ \ }

# === request_intervention — the composition action ===
#
# Given a peer, a spiral_state, and a well-formed @cyberpunk/intervention
# payload ref, discharge the intervention-request event: emit a
# content-addressed ref to the composed intervention-request Crystal
# that @cyberpunk/intervention.deploy_intervention consumes.
#
# This action is the substrate-decl'd hand-off from @paradox/spiral
# (dynamics observation) to @cyberpunk/intervention (therapeutic-payload
# deployment). Composition edge is bilateral: spiral surfaces the
# request; intervention discharges the response.
#
# Returns imperfect(ref, ref, ref): success carries the request Crystal
# ref; failure carries not-intervention-admissible / payload-malformed /
# spiral-below-threshold reasons.
#
# Requires spiral_intervention_admissible bilateral to discharge Pass.
#
# Sentinel: `paradox=spiral-request-intervention`.
request_intervention(p: peer, ctx: spiral_state, payload: ref) -> imperfect(ref, ref, ref)
requires spiral_admissible(p, ctx)
requires spiral_targets_wound_or_pre_wound(p, ctx)
requires spiral_intervention_admissible(p, ctx, payload)
{ \ }

